police in London say they suspect  terrorism after a man crashed his car  outside the houses of parliament the car  hit some pedestrians they ran into and  then it ran into a security barrier this  morning two people were injured now this  happened a few hundred yards from the  scene of a deadly terrorist attack  nearly 18 months ago Debora patta is on  the scene with the latest Deborah good  morning good morning here at Westminster  the area is in lockdown police have  cordoned off all roads around the houses  of parliament in what is being treated  as a terrorist attack it took just  minutes for London police to arrive on  the scene guns drawn they surrounded the  car arrest of the driver and led him  away in handcuffs security cameras  captured the moment the car hit a group  of cyclists before ramming into a  security barrier one bystander said he  saw one of the cyclists get up and  attempt to chase the car ambulance  services treats at least two people on  the scene before taking them to hospital  but no life-threatening injuries were  reported  Scotland Yard says no one else was in  the car and the suspect is not  cooperating with the investigation  now Parliament is in recess here so most  lawmakers were not at work today  normally this area would have been a lot  busier during rush hour traffic when the  incident occurred  fionna good to know that no one was  seriously injured Debora patta in London  thank you
 

